.TH CSTRING_NEW 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_new \- create a string with default memory management (optimistic)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cstring.h>

cstr cstring_new(const char *initial);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Convenience wrapper around cstring_create_full() that uses the default
malloc/free allocators and provides no error output. Intended for call
sites where allocation failure is treated as fatal and no error string
is required.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
initial   Initial C string content, or NULL for an empty string
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns pointer to newly created cstring on success
Returns NULL on failure (no error detail is provided)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Equivalent to cstring_create_full(initial, NULL, NULL)
Use cstring_create() when an error string on failure is needed
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_create (3),
.BR cstring_create_full (3),
.BR cstring_destroy (3)
